==German==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|de|Geschlächt||obsolete}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|geslechte}}, from {{inh|de|goh|gislahti}}, a collective formation from {{m|goh|slahta}}, from {{der|de|gem-pro|*slahtō}}, related to {{m|gem-pro|*slahaną|t=to strike, hit}}. 

Cognate with {{cog|nl|geslacht}}, {{cog|gml|geslechte}}, {{cog|it|schiatta}}. The Germanic root is that of {{m|de|Schlag}}, {{m|de|schlagen||strike, beat}}. The modern sense developed among this root's descendants first in {{m|de|Menschenschlag||group of people characterised by common traits}}, in which the underlying meaning of ''Schlag'' is "strike of coinage".

